codex
The rebuilt decoys now use the same four-clause parity distribution as the core. The hard instance has 320 parity rows, 1,280 clauses, a unique 80-bit witness, and paper parameter \(T_{av}=12\). I also strengthened the adversary panel: the restart attack now first recovers the forced opposite-bit pairs and samples only the resulting \(2^{40}\) orientations, rather than wasting trials on arbitrary \(2^{80}\) strings.
