codex
Built a native Track B 3-SAT generator based on the paper’s XOR example and DEL–PPZ analysis ([full paper](https://arxiv.org/html/0906.1849v1)).

Local verification passes:

- Unique 80-bit witness by inverse generation.
- 0/200,000 random guesses.
- Seven attacks at 0/8 each.
- Reference GF(2) elimination: 420,554 operations average.
- Compact involution route: 160 XORs.
- G1–G9(c), determinism, JSON round-trip, scaling, and canonicalization pass.

Files:

- [gen_0906_1849.py](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/0906.1849/gen_0906_1849.py:1)
- [selftest_report.json](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/0906.1849/selftest_report.json:1)
- [README.md](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/0906.1849/README.md:1)
- [bare transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/0906.1849/llm_loop_transcript.jsonl:1)
- [hinted transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/0906.1849/g9_hinted_transcript.jsonl:1)
- [placebo transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/0906.1849/g9_placebo_transcript.jsonl:1)

The result is not release-ready: all three mandated harness runs received OpenRouter HTTP 403 “Key limit exceeded,” yielding zero scored oracle attempts and no `hardened` verdict. The transcripts preserve that failure honestly. A renewed `OPENROUTER_API_KEY` is required to finish Step 4.
