codex
Implemented and verified a Track B generator based on the paper’s XOR-based 3-SAT family ([arXiv:0906.1849](https://arxiv.org/abs/0906.1849)).

Key results:

- `hard` ships with 80 variables, 240 decoy parity rows, and 1,280 clauses.
- All local G1–G9(c) gates pass.
- Reference GF(2) elimination solves 8/8, as Track B requires.
- Oracle ladder: `easy` solved 2/3, `medium` 1/3, `hard` 0/3—verdict `hardened`.
- G9 hint/placebo runs were attempted but received only quota errors; this diagnostic is recorded as unavailable.
- Fixed canonicalization to cover variable relabelling, pair-member exchange, pairwise complementation, clause ordering, and cycle rotation.

Deliverables:

- [gen_0906_1849.py](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/0906.1849/gen_0906_1849.py)
- [selftest_report.json](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/0906.1849/selftest_report.json)
- [README.md](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/0906.1849/README.md)
- [llm_loop_transcript.jsonl](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/0906.1849/llm_loop_transcript.jsonl)
- [g9_hinted_transcript.jsonl](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/0906.1849/g9_hinted_transcript.jsonl)
- [g9_placebo_transcript.jsonl](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/0906.1849/g9_placebo_transcript.jsonl)
- [.meta.json](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/0906.1849/.meta.json)

All Python and JSON artifacts parse successfully.
